86663582eb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442982 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3y-z-11 & =0 \\\\ -4x+3y-z & =11 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ -4(-2+3t)+3(1+2t)-(4-6t) & =11 \\\\ 8-12t+3+6t-4+6t & =11 \\\\ 7 & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186444803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1045 "Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186444802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444798 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "024faa8c-8ac3-506b-9b2c-333430674981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444799 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444799 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0052f793-89f1-5c58-93a6-48098b6aceba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444799 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186362392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444800 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444803 #edb/ref 1